## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design end-to-end encrypted, multi-party voice with dynamic membership, offline resilience, and production-ready media handling. It probes WebRTC, key management, and data persistence trade-offs across devices.

## Key Concepts

- WebRTC for multi-party audio and signaling flow
- End-to-end encryption with per-device keys and a group-key envelope
- Nightly key rotation via Android Keystore and secure key derivation
- Offline transcripts using Room; offline-first UX
- Audio quality: jitter buffer, AGC, and network adaptivity

